# Day 1 — System Design Document

## 1. User Query Flow
When a user types “wireless headphones”:
1. The query goes to the Search Service.
2. The system retrieves candidate products using keyword matching.
3. The Feature Builder collects product signals — price, rating, popularity.
4. The Ranker scores products based on user type (Budget or Quality).
5. Products are sorted and shown.
6. User clicks are recorded for feedback and evaluation using NDCG@K.

## 2. Data Requirements
### Products Table
product_id, name, category, price, rating, popularity, description

### User Table
user_id, persona_type (Budget / Quality), past_clicks/purchases

### Events Table
event_id, user_id, product_id, query, clicked, timestamp

## 3. Data Flow
products.csv → retrieval + feature building  
user.csv → identify persona and apply weights  
events.csv → created after ranking, used for feedback

## 4. Build Order
Start with synthetic data generation for products and users.
